han 90% of patients</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>2006</year><volume>129</volume><fpage>1470</fpage><lpage>80 Epub 2006 Apr 18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16621918</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/brain/awl077</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ibarra</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Murayama</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Minami</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ichihara</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kikuchi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Noguchi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayashi</surname><given-names>YK</given-names></name><name><surname>Ochiai</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishino</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Malignant hyperthermia in Japan: mutation screening of the entire ryanodine receptor type 1 gene coding region by direct sequencing</article-title><source>Anesthesiology</source><year>2006</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>1146</fpage><lpage>1154</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16732084</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000542-200606000-00008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shepherd</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Halsall</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopkins</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>RYR1 mutations in UK central core disease patients: more than just the C-terminal transmembrane region of the RYR1 ge